I am not best with testing but i think this function doesn't support changing version of the etcd client version. https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/blob/8a0147c8825ddd6afa56fd3e647e2d659683483c/staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/storage/etcd3/testserver/test_server.go#L84
For now we use `clientv3.Client` as input value of ` func checkVersion(c *clientv3.Client, dialTimeOut time.Duration) (err error)`, maybe i change that to some interface and implement `Status` method that use to check version of etcd for that interface and test the whole function like that.
Also for testing these parts
```
consistentListFromCacheEnabled := utilfeature.DefaultFeatureGate.Enabled(genericfeatures.ConsistentListFromCache)
	if consistentListFromCacheEnabled {
		if err := checkVersion(etcdClient, dialTimeout); err != nil {
			// disable the feature
			rerr := utilfeature.DefaultMutableFeatureGate.OverrideDefault(genericfeatures.ConsistentListFromCache, false)
			if rerr != nil {
				return nil, fmt.Errorf("failed disabling ConsistentListFromCache flag, %w", rerr)
			}
			klog.ErrorS(err, "Warning: Using ConsistentListFromCache requires newer etcd version, disabling the ConsistentListFromCache feature flag")
		}
	}
```
maybe i move them to a new function and test that function with some unit test to avoid writing test for whole `newETCD3Client`.
I would appreciate you're opinion about this. @serathius @wojtek-t @aojea
